@startuml
title BellLap session state machine (F04)
hide empty description

[*] --> Setup

state "SETUP\nlive preview, finish line" as Setup
state "STANDBY\nscreen dimmed, listening for bell" as Standby
state "ARMING\n10 s delay" as Arming
state "ARMED\ncamera on, watching for flag" as Armed
state "ACQUISITION\nrecording + crossings" as Acq {
    state "flag seen" as FlagSeen
    state "flag absent\n(timer running)" as FlagAbsent
    [*] --> FlagSeen : FlagSeen (from ARMED)
    [*] --> FlagAbsent : RecordNow (from ARMED)
    FlagSeen --> FlagAbsent : FlagLost
    FlagAbsent --> FlagSeen : FlagSeen
    FlagSeen --> FlagSeen : CrossingDetected / PlayCrossingBeep
    FlagAbsent --> FlagAbsent : CrossingDetected / PlayCrossingBeep
}
state "REVIEW overlay\n(session keeps running underneath)" as Review

Setup --> Standby : StandbyRequested
Standby --> Arming : BellDetected | BellNow\n/ RestoreBrightness
Arming --> Armed : ArmDelayElapsed\n/ PlayArmedBeeps
Armed --> Acq : FlagSeen / StartRecording
Armed --> Acq : RecordNow / StartRecording

Acq --> Armed : FlagAbsentTimeout (flag absent) | Stop\n/ StopRecording, PlayStandDownChime

Standby --> Setup : Stop / RestoreBrightness
Arming --> Setup : Stop
Armed --> Setup : Stop

Setup --> Review : EnterReview
Standby --> Review : EnterReview
Armed --> Review : EnterReview
Review --> Setup : ExitReview (entered from SETUP)
Review --> Standby : ExitReview (entered from STANDBY)
Review --> Armed : ExitReview (entered from ARMED)

note bottom of Review
  Not allowed from ARMING or ACQUISITION.
  Bell, flag and timer events still apply
  to the underlying session while reviewing,
  and ExitReview returns to its current state.
end note

note bottom of Acq
  FlagAbsentTimeout is ignored while the flag is seen.
  Default timeout 15 s (configurable).
  Any event not shown is ignored and logged.
end note
@enduml
